# Warden's native checks by parity: #126 the mark and Shadow Pursuit.
# Warden a against Warden b; syntax and checks: smashcraft:docs/native-bot-session.md.
#! chat -dev quick hero warden
# b dashes in to about 280 away, within Shadow Pursuit's reach; eda5e178f2 made Maiev grippier, so b holds the dash 3 frames (variant run 39025469042).
40 b stick -1 0
43 b stick 0 0
# Counterplay: b's held shield takes Shadow Strike, so no mark.
50 b shield 1
60 a tap X 2
140 b shield 0
# Shadow Strike marks b.
200 a tap X 2
# Shadow Pursuit appears behind the marked b and slashes.
290 a stick 1 0
290 a tap X 2
291 a stick 0 0
# The mark is spent: the next side special, back toward b, is the plain Pursuit Lunge.
440 a stick -1 0
440 a tap X 2
441 a stick 0 0
# Fan of Knives.
# View held a second: the first of two moments the parity check replays.
500 a press VIEW
570 a release VIEW
600 a stick 0 -1
600 a tap X 2
601 a stick 0 0
# Expected, frame by frame (headless run of this script):
#! expect a 60 special 13 form 0
#! absent b 60-199 damage
#! expect a 200 special 13 form 0
# 1ed1f22499 (#414 step 3) set Shadow Strike to 3.816 and Pursuit to 7.633; the lighter hits shorten hitlag, so Pursuit ends a frame sooner.
#! expect b 229 damage 3.816
#! expect b 289 damage 4.816 hitlag 0 hitstun 0
#! expect a 290 special 14 form 4
#! expect b 307 damage 12.449
#! expect a 333 special 0 form 4 action-frame 0 x 133.715
#! expect a 440 special 14 form 0
#! expect b 450 damage 20.082
#! expect a 600 special 16 form 0
# 6c432ce445 made Fan of Knives a frame-one shine for 6.106, so it hits on 600 and poisons from there.
#! expect b 600 damage 26.188
#! expect b 660 damage 27.188 hitlag 0 hitstun 0
1000 a press VIEW
1070 a release VIEW
